{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there","id":785021,"title":"How many nobles are there?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-12T15:23:29-08:00","id":785021,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon2.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How many nobles are there?","content":"With so many houses the sihde must be the kith with most members. Have I got it wrong or are over half the changelings sihde?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T20:09:12-08:00","id":785141,"title":"","content":"Not all nobles are sidhe, and not all members of a House's retinue are nobles. Obviously only nobles are accorded full membership of a House, but a lot of their apparent size, power and reach comes from their retainers, commoner and enchanted alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:32:25-08:00","id":785242,"title":"","content":"or the Kithain are the most populous supernatural after wraiths, they do have much larger geographic groupings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T13:51:42-08:00","id":785551,"title":"","content":"Did we ever get an official number on how many changelings there were in the world? My feeling is that it'd be easy for large numbers of them to hide among us, as their faerie nature and chimerical reality are both pretty much invisible to everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T20:49:43-08:00","id":785727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=785551#post785551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever get an official number on how many changelings there were in the world? My feeling is that it'd be easy for large numbers of them to hide among us, as their faerie nature and chimerical reality are both pretty much invisible to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just assumed their base organization requires very large numbers, each king has multiple dukes who have multiple counts who have multiple barons and on and so forth each is out number signficantly by the commoners. I'd put them just south of wraith levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T09:38:37-08:00","id":786760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=785727#post785727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I just assumed their base organization requires very large numbers, each king has multiple dukes who have multiple counts who have multiple barons and on and so forth each is out number signficantly by the commoners. I'd put them just south of wraith levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's gotta be millions of wraiths, though (not all of them sentient, true). Isn't there something like a million in London alone? The world can't be that teeming with changelings can it?<br /> <br /> Or maybe it is. I guess they can hide in plain sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T00:16:43-08:00","id":787190,"title":"","content":"I think there are not as many changelings as wraiths, but if you'll count every chimerical creature - well, than it could be close to wraith numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10123-equeslilia","name":"equeslilia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T03:10:32-08:00","id":787248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>equeslilia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=787190#post787190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are not as many changelings as wraiths, but if you'll count every chimerical creature - well, than it could be close to wraith numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It must exceed it, I quess. I think there is almost as many Chimera as &quot;Umbroods&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T05:29:28-08:00","id":787288,"title":"","content":"There are countless chimerical creatures. A lot don't last more than hours or weeks -- they're born, their parent dream ends, they fade away, or Banality wears them down if they don't have a Glamour source to replenish themselves. Chimera are everywhere, even in the urban Dreaming. They're constantly being birthed from the minds of mortal Dreamers, changelings and other assorted beings. Changelings aren't chimera, though, so you can't really count the two together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T21:01:04-08:00","id":787825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=786760#post786760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there's gotta be millions of wraiths, though (not all of them sentient, true). Isn't there something like a million in London alone? The world can't be that teeming with changelings can it?<br /> <br /> Or maybe it is. I guess they can hide in plain sight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wraith numbers are big, then you have vampire numbers that put it at roughly 6k. Vampires have a fairly basic structure of small almost tribal level groups based on each city with some group alliances splitting them up roughly across the world. There isn't a huge degree of complicated social grouping based on their size. Similarly changing Breeds are generally focused on small levels, you have Septs and Maybe &quot;The Nation&quot; or &quot;The hengeyokai&quot; etc. Here we also see the base build of the culture around a single place of power with as I said some out growth.<br /> <br /> Now here's where it gets complicated with the changelings, a Knight or Squire may not have a Freehold(but even they might hold in the name of their lord), but a landless baron is rare. So lets assume a barons Holdings are on par with a Kindred or KJ Court or a Changing Breed Sept. So I assume there's 10x+ as many changelings as there are Vamps/Cb which puts them south of wraiths in numbers.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:26:30-08:00","id":787935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=787825#post787825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wraith numbers are big, then you have vampire numbers that put it at roughly 6k. Vampires have a fairly basic structure of small almost tribal level groups based on each city with some group alliances splitting them up roughly across the world. There isn't a huge degree of complicated social grouping based on their size. Similarly changing Breeds are generally focused on small levels, you have Septs and Maybe &amp;quot;The Nation&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;The hengeyokai&amp;quot; etc. Here we also see the base build of the culture around a single place of power with as I said some out growth.<br /> <br /> Now here's where it gets complicated with the changelings, a Knight or Squire may not have a Freehold(but even they might hold in the name of their lord), but a landless baron is rare. So lets assume a barons Holdings are on par with a Kindred or KJ Court or a Changing Breed Sept. So I assume there's 10x+ as many changelings as there are Vamps/Cb which puts them south of wraiths in numbers.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's 1 vampire for every 100,000 mortals, so there are 60,000 in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T04:35:32-08:00","id":788663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=787935#post787935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's 1 vampire for every 100,000 mortals, so there are 60,000 in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That was a typo on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T09:45:23-08:00","id":789792,"title":"","content":"Its not canon (they never gave concrete numbers), but I've usually ran with 1 Changeling for every 20k people. Putting them at roughly 5 times as many Changelings as Vampires.<br /> The nature of the Mists makes keeping Changelings hidden is incredibly easy, to the point of most splats thinking Changelings are near extinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T13:59:20-08:00","id":789911,"title":"","content":"I think the best answer is &quot;there are as many changelings as you need there to be&quot;. Maybe there are hundreds of thousands across the world. Maybe there are only hundreds. I don't think there are canon concrete numbers, so pick a number that works for your setting and games, and go with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T18:06:18-08:00","id":790012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=789911#post789911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best answer is &quot;there are as many changelings as you need there to be&quot;. Maybe there are hundreds of thousands across the world. Maybe there are only hundreds. I don't think there are canon concrete numbers, so pick a number that works for your setting and games, and go with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it needs high numbers because you have Kingdoms, and huge battles a High king of a group in the hundreds should litterally know everyone there... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T19:50:51-08:00","id":790056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=790012#post790012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it needs high numbers because you have Kingdoms, and huge battles a High king of a group in the hundreds should litterally know everyone there...</div> </div> </div> </div>For a standard game, sure. Not everyone likes to play straight out of the box, though. Some games are run with hacked settings. A CtD worldwide disaster game is going to have very different numbers than one dealing with court politics set in the Kingdom of Apples. Some people like having changelings rarer, some like to have them more numerous. Pick what works for your game, a number you like for your setting, and use that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T20:29:52-08:00","id":790066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=790056#post790056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a standard game, sure. Not everyone likes to play straight out of the box, though. Some games are run with hacked settings. A CtD worldwide disaster game is going to have very different numbers than one dealing with court politics set in the Kingdom of Apples. Some people like having changelings rarer, some like to have them more numerous. Pick what works for your game, a number you like for your setting, and use that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is fair, but I think its worth trying to figure what the &quot;base&quot; assumptions are before you start hacking. Or at least I do. Of course I find &quot;Court/sept rougly have this many x&quot; is far more useful than the how many supernaturals to humans one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:16:05-08:00","id":791116,"title":"","content":"So a house has a number of nobles, say 30-60+ so that it can have a number if lords and representatives and branches for infighting. Each noble has somewhere between 4-20+ retainers, servants and the like, that gives 120-1200 retainers. A house should have some armed forces to back it up, say 90-300 (or 3-5 bodyguards/soldiers per noble). Any noble in the house with a domain can draw upon their vassals for aid, lets say 20 additional changelings per noble, that gives 600-1200 additional changlings.<br /> If we take my low estimates we get 240 changelings per noble house (840 with vassals). The high estimates give 2760 changelings with vassals per house.<br /> Does this sound reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T20:42:34-08:00","id":791944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/785021-how-many-nobles-are-there?p=791116#post791116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a house has a number of nobles, say 30-60+ so that it can have a number if lords and representatives and branches for infighting. Each noble has somewhere between 4-20+ retainers, servants and the like, that gives 120-1200 retainers. A house should have some armed forces to back it up, say 90-300 (or 3-5 bodyguards/soldiers per noble). Any noble in the house with a domain can draw upon their vassals for aid, lets say 20 additional changelings per noble, that gives 600-1200 additional changlings.<br /> If we take my low estimates we get 240 changelings per noble house (840 with vassals). The high estimates give 2760 changelings with vassals per house.<br /> Does this sound reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be approximately 10,920 and 35,880 with vassals (based on 840 or 2760 changelings in each of the 13 houses). Maybe the newer houses only have half the numbers of the older houses, although it's been 20 years, so they may have caught up. I'm leaving out the 14th House intentionally, because they're something different.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I'll take some liberties and make some sweeping assumptions here...<br /> <br /> If we go slap bang in the middle, we get 23,400 fae in houses. Let's say that the ratio of commoners to nobles is 2:1 (I can't remember what the books say), so that gives us 70,200 Western Kithain. That probably doesn't account for the Gallain, Thallain, etc, that live here in the Western world. Plus, the Western kiths probably only account for about a third of the world's fae population, if that (the kiths presented in the core game are from a very narrow range of cultural backgrounds). There could easily be 250,000+ fae in the world... (Running the numbers, you get 210,600 fae worldwide, or 1:28,490 fae to humans.)<br /> <br /> If you go with the higher end, you'd get 322,920 fae, which is 1:18,580. If you go with the lower end, you get 98,280 fae, which is 1:61,050.<br /> <br /> The 1:20,000 figure others have used actually seems kind of realistic. Although you can also opt for the same number as vampires (1:60,000) if you want to be conservative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T18:01:03-08:00","id":792888,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have always assumed there were more Changelings than just about every other supernatural in the WoD, but they have a much shorter lifespan. By the time they are in their 30's, I imagine there are only a fraction of the original population that hasn't been lost. Plus, children's dreams are much stronger and more pervasive than the dreams of adults, which means to me that there are bound to be plenty of child Changelings who simply never become aware of their nature. They may go crazy or they may lose sight of it after a short while. Maybe they just grow up and face the &quot;real&quot; world. Either way, I imagine that there are plenty of Changeling children, fewer wildlings, and even fewer grumps. Courts are definitely going to be skewed toward the young and passionate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:54:11-08:00","id":797225,"title":"","content":"Seems to me the OP as mostly wondering about the Sidhe/Commoner ratio than hard numbers. If that is the case, it's never been that clear either. The Sidhe were supposed to be in numerical inferiority during the Accordance War, and it's logical that rulers should be less numerous than their subjects, but then we have things like the Commoner pogroms in Neustria being mentioned, that muddle things a bit. It becomes even fuzzier if you take into account the merfolk who are supposedly all nobles, the Ali'i, the Oba and the Kamuii.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T04:58:21-08:00","id":797278,"title":"","content":"1:10 nobles:commoners?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}